{"artifacts":{"architecture-governor.json":{"sha256":"9bf2a4ca7963d3cdaa32ee667a06953579180b5bcc682d6c4818cdf89a2e0cff","text":"{\"context_sha256\":\"39c42d261f92dada9ab63dad4d2322fb70b6f50a830091bf1ee291dae77246d8\",\"contract_sha256\":\"8d3107a78e3f12727a0f2996edbd07a6065e665ddeb933fbc1f59b696b2f7093\",\"convergence\":\"improves\",\"debts\":[\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\"],\"decision\":\"proceed\",\"design_sha256\":\"1dde921412b925acabb450b0c52b348151dbaa87a9115ba3fce18b957a342451\",\"migrations\":[\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\"policy_sha256\":\"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add\",\"principles\":[\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\",\"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\"rationale\":[\"Seam is named and singular: all ten contract behaviors map to the existing CitationModal component interface, observable via render + document.activeElement without reaching into internals.\",\"The design deepens the existing module: focus entry and focus return are added behind the unchanged two-prop interface (citation, onClose) with no new props, params, or knobs.\",\"Callers stay unorchestrated: ChatArea.handleCitationClick only sets selectedCitation state; the modal owns capture, entry, and restore internally, so no caller must sequence focus steps.\",\"No parallel abstraction is created: extending CitationModal in place is preferred over a new useFocusReturn hook or focus-util module that would serve exactly one caller today (speculative extension point per ARCH-DEEP-MODULES).\",\"Layer direction is respected: no new import edges; modal UI behavior stays inside a components-layer file as ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES requires, and the only external import remains the existing Citation type from lib/api.\",\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS direction holds: production changes are confined to CitationModal.tsx, ChatArea.tsx and Sidebar.tsx are not touched, so the large-component hotspot does not grow.\",\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA no-growth holds: ChatArea.tsx appears only as context (caller wiring), not as a planned change file, so its byte footprint is unchanged.\",\"Guard behaviors AC-7 through AC-10 are already pinned by existing tests in CitationModal.test.tsx (Escape called once, close button, backdrop target check, embed start/autoplay and external t param), and the design leaves those code paths untouched.\",\"jsdom honours .focus() and document.activeElement, so AC-1 through AC-6 are provable through the public seam; the isConnected guard makes AC-6 deterministic rather than browser-dependent.\",\"Capture-then-focus ordering inside the single mount effect keeps the modal's own close button from ever becoming the restore target and also keeps React StrictMode's simulated remount correct.\",\"Exact planned files (CitationModal.tsx + CitationModal.test.tsx, no new files) match the design's allowed-file set, so kernel commit scope is satisfiable without enlargement.\",\"Convergence improves on a multi-ticket horizon: accessibility behavior lands at the component that owns it, reducing any future temptation to add focus orchestration into ChatArea, the no-growth hotspot.\"],\"required_changes\":[],\"source_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"architecture-governor.raw.json":{"sha256":"fc5fc4a1c9bd0de5eeec096e87cfaaa845526df6ee32b5ae6c8d7e1049d9de6b","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"decision\": \"proceed\",\n  \"convergence\": \"improves\",\n  \"principles\": [\"ARCH-DEEP-MODULES\", \"ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES\"],\n  \"migrations\": [\"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS\"],\n  \"debts\": [\"DEBT-CHAT-AREA\"],\n  \"rationale\": [\n    \"Seam is named and singular: all ten contract behaviors map to the existing CitationModal component interface, observable via render + document.activeElement without reaching into internals.\",\n    \"The design deepens the existing module: focus entry and focus return are added behind the unchanged two-prop interface (citation, onClose) with no new props, params, or knobs.\",\n    \"Callers stay unorchestrated: ChatArea.handleCitationClick only sets selectedCitation state; the modal owns capture, entry, and restore internally, so no caller must sequence focus steps.\",\n    \"No parallel abstraction is created: extending CitationModal in place is preferred over a new useFocusReturn hook or focus-util module that would serve exactly one caller today (speculative extension point per ARCH-DEEP-MODULES).\",\n    \"Layer direction is respected: no new import edges; modal UI behavior stays inside a components-layer file as ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES requires, and the only external import remains the existing Citation type from lib/api.\",\n    \"MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS direction holds: production changes are confined to CitationModal.tsx, ChatArea.tsx and Sidebar.tsx are not touched, so the large-component hotspot does not grow.\",\n    \"DEBT-CHAT-AREA no-growth holds: ChatArea.tsx appears only as context (caller wiring), not as a planned change file, so its byte footprint is unchanged.\",\n    \"Guard behaviors AC-7 through AC-10 are already pinned by existing tests in CitationModal.test.tsx (Escape called once, close button, backdrop target check, embed start/autoplay and external t param), and the design leaves those code paths untouched.\",\n    \"jsdom honours .focus() and document.activeElement, so AC-1 through AC-6 are provable through the public seam; the isConnected guard makes AC-6 deterministic rather than browser-dependent.\",\n    \"Capture-then-focus ordering inside the single mount effect keeps the modal's own close button from ever becoming the restore target and also keeps React StrictMode's simulated remount correct.\",\n    \"Exact planned files (CitationModal.tsx + CitationModal.test.tsx, no new files) match the design's allowed-file set, so kernel commit scope is satisfiable without enlargement.\",\n    \"Convergence improves on a multi-ticket horizon: accessibility behavior lands at the component that owns it, reducing any future temptation to add focus orchestration into ChatArea, the no-growth hotspot.\"\n  ],\n  \"required_changes\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Fresh-governor review; no edits made to code or prior artifacts. Verified the applicable policy sets against architecture.json myself and they match the kernel-provided lists verbatim: ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES via app/frontend/src prefix on every context/planned file, ARCH-DEEP-MODULES via the app prefix, MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS and DEBT-CHAT-AREA only via context-only ChatArea.tsx; no backend or factory paths appear. Contract sha256 matches the validated value (8d3107a7...7093) and the contract contains zero ambiguities. Judgement on the two design choices I considered but do not require: (1) a useFocusReturn hook in app/frontend/src/hooks would be the natural extraction if a second dialog ever needs focus return, but with a single caller today it is a speculative seam, so keeping the logic inside CitationModal is the correct deep-module call; revisit only when a second consumer actually exists. (2) The focus effect should be mount-only ([] deps, like the existing body-scroll lock) rather than keyed on onClose, to avoid cleanup/restore churn on every parent re-render; this is implementation advice, not a structural demand. Known accepted risks carried from the contract, not blockers: real-browser iframe focus steal after the YouTube embed loads is out of scope (e2e should assert focus immediately after open), restore-target drift if foreign code moves focus between click and effect (nothing in the app currently does), and the accessible name 'Close' is both the seam selector and the accessibility contract so it must not be renamed. Enter/Space on the newly focused close button closing the modal is a behaviour improvement consistent with the pinned Escape-once test, which still passes because only one document keydown listener exists.\"\n}\n"},"context.enriched.json":{"sha256":"cd1000bfd70b129d70f36238fbed2156d189e654a951dfaa9525cf3e30d6d736","text":"{\"adrs\":[],\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx#citationChip\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"[derived] app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\"],\"contract_sha256\":\"8d3107a78e3f12727a0f2996edbd07a6065e665ddeb933fbc1f59b696b2f7093\",\"deterministic_impact\":{\"callers\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\"],\"derived_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/App.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-refreshConversationsRef.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-strictmode-first-send.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.test.tsx\"],\"mode\":\"context\",\"public_interfaces\":[{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":9,\"name\":\"formatTimestamp\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":16,\"name\":\"CitationModal\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":163,\"name\":\"Message\",\"public\":true},{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx\",\"language\":\"typescript\",\"line\":292,\"name\":\"ChatArea\",\"public\":true}],\"sha256\":\"47f85544585e1fa4bc2ccbedfeb8e16122e4f97d609d9ee4cc3d2e83c8ee26ec\",\"symbols\":[{\"file\":\"app/frontend/src/components/Citati