eCitationClick\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/Message.tsx#citationChip\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-handleCitationClick.test.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"The opener is captured from document.activeElement before focus is moved to the close button, within the same mount effect, so the modal's own focus-entry target can never become the restore target.\",\n    \"Focus restoration happens only when the captured opener is an HTMLElement still connected to the document (el.isConnected); otherwise the cleanup is a no-op and no detached node is focused.\",\n    \"No focus trap is added; Tab behaviour beyond focus entry and focus return is unchanged.\",\n    \"Production changes are confined to app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx; Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, the backend, authentication, owner-private conversation handling and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\",\n    \"Existing close paths (Escape, close button, backdrop), body scroll lock, iframe/external URL derivation and transcript-snippet rendering keep their current code and tests.\",\n    \"No new dependencies are introduced: vitest, @testing-library/react and @testing-library/jest-dom are already installed in app/frontend.\",\n    \"The focus-entry seam selects the close button by role 'button' with accessible name 'Close' (aria-label); that label is the accessibility contract and must not be renamed.\"\n  ],\n  \"adrs\": [],\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"CitationModal.tsx already has the three effects the contract pins (Escape keydown on document with single onClose call, body scroll lock, and the close/backdrop handlers with e.target === e.currentTarget); the change adds one mount effect (capture opener from document.activeElement, focus the close button) and one unmount cleanup (restore focus when opener is an HTMLElement and el.isConnected). Message.tsx#citationChip renders the opener as a <button>, so document.activeElement at open time is a real button element. ChatArea.tsx line ~788 renders <CitationModal citation={selectedCitation} onClose={() => setSelectedCitation(null)} />. Dynamous citations bypass the modal entirely via ChatArea.handleCitationClick. Existing CitationModal.test.tsx already pins: Escape fires onClose exactly once, close button and backdrop close, iframe src with start=<startSeconds>&autoplay=1, external link t=<startSeconds>s, Video unavailable paths (invalid URL, empty v, relative URL), body scroll lock. No docs/adr directory exists in this repository.\"\n}\n"},"design.json":{"sha256":"1dde921412b925acabb450b0c52b348151dbaa87a9115ba3fce18b957a342451","text":"{\"ac_mapping\":{\"AC-1\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-10\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-2\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-3\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-4\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-5\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-6\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-7\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-8\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"AC-9\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"]},\"allowed_new_files\":[],\"context_sha256\":\"39c42d261f92dada9ab63dad4d2322fb70b6f50a830091bf1ee291dae77246d8\",\"contract_sha256\":\"8d3107a78e3f12727a0f2996edbd07a6065e665ddeb933fbc1f59b696b2f7093\",\"data_flows\":[\"citation chip button click (ChatArea) -> CitationModal mount -> mount effect captures document.activeElement as opener -> close button ('Close') receives focus\",\"Escape keydown / close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmount -> unmount cleanup restores focus to opener when it is an HTMLElement and el.isConnected, else no-op\"],\"invariants\":[\"The opener is captured from document.activeElement before focus is moved to the close button, within the same mount effect, so the modal's own focus-entry target can never become the restore target.\",\"Focus restoration happens only when the captured opener is an HTMLElement still connected to the document (el.isConnected); otherwise the cleanup is a no-op and no detached node is focused.\",\"No focus trap is added; Tab behaviour beyond focus entry and focus return is unchanged.\",\"Existing close paths (Escape single onClose call, close button, backdrop with e.target === e.currentTarget), body scroll lock, iframe embedUrl start=<startSeconds>&autoplay=1 and externalUrl t=<startSeconds>s derivation, and transcript-snippet pre-wrap rendering keep their current code and tests.\",\"The focus-entry target is the in-dialog close button found by role 'button' with accessible name 'Close'; that aria-label is unchanged.\",\"No new dependencies are introduced.\"],\"modules\":[\"CitationModal (keyboard focus entry + focus return, added to the existing modal component)\"],\"planned_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\",\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\"],\"public_interfaces\":[\"CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element\"],\"seams\":[\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"design.raw.json":{"sha256":"0354b27bddb5d2dc470359d6152f36a2d12abbf1023681ec59c0845466416dd1","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"modules\": [\n    \"CitationModal (keyboard focus entry + focus return, added to the existing modal component)\"\n  ],\n  \"seams\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n  ],\n  \"public_interfaces\": [\n    \"CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"The opener is captured from document.activeElement before focus is moved to the close button, within the same mount effect, so the modal's own focus-entry target can never become the restore target.\",\n    \"Focus restoration happens only when the captured opener is an HTMLElement still connected to the document (el.isConnected); otherwise the cleanup is a no-op and no detached node is focused.\",\n    \"No focus trap is added; Tab behaviour beyond focus entry and focus return is unchanged.\",\n    \"Existing close paths (Escape single onClose call, close button, backdrop with e.target === e.currentTarget), body scroll lock, iframe embedUrl start=<startSeconds>&autoplay=1 and externalUrl t=<startSeconds>s derivation, and transcript-snippet pre-wrap rendering keep their current code and tests.\",\n    \"The focus-entry target is the in-dialog close button found by role 'button' with accessible name 'Close'; that aria-label is unchanged.\",\n    \"No new dependencies are introduced.\"\n  ],\n  \"data_flows\": [\n    \"citation chip button click (ChatArea) -> CitationModal mount -> mount effect captures document.activeElement as opener -> close button ('Close') receives focus\",\n    \"Escape keydown / close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmount -> unmount cleanup restores focus to opener when it is an HTMLElement and el.isConnected, else no-op\"\n  ],\n  \"ac_mapping\": {\n    \"AC-1\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-2\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-3\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-4\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-5\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-6\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-7\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-8\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-9\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"],\n    \"AC-10\": [\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"]\n  },\n  \"planned_files\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"allowed_new_files\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Smallest deep-module design: one existing component, one new mount effect and one new unmount cleanup inside it. Mount effect: capture document.activeElement, then focus the close button (via a ref on the existing aria-label='Close' button — no new DOM, no label change). Unmount cleanup: if the captured opener is an HTMLElement and .isConnected, call .focus() on it. Guard ACs 7-10 are pinned by existing tests in CitationModal.test.tsx and must keep passing; new tests for AC-1..AC-6 are added to the same existing test file (no new test files, no production changes outside CitationModal.tsx). planned_files includes the existing test file because new assertions for focus entry/return are added there; allowed_new_files is empty.\"\n}\n"},"frontier.json":{"sha256":"17af29059e2658c809c2485d3d1b7109f754e46c051a398cbabf31bd0ba5d3c8","text":"{\"accepted\":true,\"blockers\":[{\"issue\":181,\"state\":\"CLOSED\"}],\"issue\":189,\"ready\":true,\"ticket_sha256\":\"5d8fbab973959533562b0e61687d978fd962f97ce65aa66294a1141e7240945d\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue-frontier.json":{"sha256":"406060794d16c99d712f10f475e2ac0ddcd36d9d22cc6eccf5aa9b24e00bd6de","text":"{\"blockers\":[{\"issue\":181,\"state\":\"CLOSED\"}],\"fetched_at\":\"2026-09-16T00:18:20Z\",\"issue\":{\"author\":{\"is_bot\":true,\"login\":\"app/shaishibear-dark-factory\"},\"body\":\"<!-- dark-factory-programme:d809b087a48a5d3a634286dc5f303d90ce119139a799ace0a122a7e244766b00:keyboard -->\\n\\nViewers can read the cited transcript and use the citation modal with the keyboard.\\n\\nSpecification: citation-inspection v1\\nSpecification SHA256: 2ebd0a37d772950d9364c1178f7c6330c6c0cd12367a479ef1eebc7a66f0bbb5\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- focus-entry (keyboard): Opening the citation modal moves keyboard focus to a usable control inside it.\\n- focus-return (keyboard): Closing the citation modal returns keyboard focus to the opener when it remains in the document.\\n\\n## Hard constraints\\n- Preserve existing video playback, timestamp links, Escape, close-button and backdrop close behavior.\\n- Preserve authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit.\\n- All existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes or external dependencies.\\n\\nBlocked by: #181\\n\\nThis is a compiled programme candidate. Normal triage and all existing factory proof and permission rules apply.\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"a2eeef\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEU9Q\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\"}],\"number\":189,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-15T22:05:32Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ShaishiBear/dark-factory-2.0/issues/189\"},\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue.json":{"sha256":"39407aea6d529502af72bd80ca9b39b5bc0433c841d4bd11e505a0782e1cc6f3","text":"{\"author\":{\"is_bot\":true,\"login\":\"app/shaishibear-dark-factory\"},\"body\":\"<!-- dark-factory-programme:d809b087a48a5d3a634286dc5f303d90ce119139a799ace0a122a7e244766b00:keyboard -->\\n\\nViewers can read the cited transcript and use the citation modal with the keyboard.\\n\\nSpecification: citation-inspection v1\\nSpecification SHA256: 2ebd0a37d772950d9364c1178f7c6330c6c0cd12367a479ef1eebc7a66f0bbb5\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- focus-entry (keyboard): Opening the citation modal moves keyboard focus to a usable control inside it.\\n- focus-return (keyboard): Closing the citation modal returns keyboard focus to the opener when it remains in the document.\\n\\n## Hard constraints\\n- Preserve existing video playback, timestamp links, Escape, close-button and backdrop close behavior.\\n- Preserve authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit.\\n- All existing independent proof and permission rules remain mandatory.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes or external dependencies.\\n\\nBlocked by: #181\\n\\nThis is a compiled programme candidate. Normal triage and all existing factory proof and permission rules apply.\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"a2eeef\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEU9Q\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\"}],\"number\":189,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-15T22:05:32Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ShaishiBear/dark-factory-2.0/issues/189\"}\n"},"task-contract.json":{"sha256":"8d3107a78e3f12727a0f2996edbd07a6065e665ddeb933fbc1f59b696b2f7093","text":"{\"ambiguities\":[],\"behaviors\":[{\"given\":\"the citation modal is mounted, having been opened from a citation chip button that currently has keyboard focus\",\"id\":\"AC-1\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\",\"then\":\"keyboard focus is on the in-dialog close button (role 'button', accessible name 'Close'), a usable control inside the aria-modal dialog, not left on the chip behind the dialog\",\"when\":\"CitationModal renders\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is mounted for a citation whose video_url yields no usable v parameter (the 'Video unavailable' path: no iframe and no 'Open on YouTube' link rendered)\",\"id\":\"AC-2\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\",\"then\":\"the close button still receives keyboard focus — focus-entry does not depend on the iframe or external link being present\",\"when\":\"CitationModal renders\"},{\"given\":\"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it (chip + modal rendered together, mirroring ChatArea's wiring)\",\"id\":\"AC-3\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"then\":\"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\",\"when\":\"the modal is closed via Escape (document keydown Escape → onClose → modal unmounts)\"},{\"given\":\"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it\",\"id\":\"AC-4\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"then\":\"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\",\"when\":\"the modal is closed via the × close button click\"},{\"given\":\"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it\",\"id\":\"AC-5\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"then\":\"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\",\"when\":\"the modal is closed via a backdrop click (click on the outer overlay, not the dialog body)\"},{\"given\":\"the opener chip button has been removed from the document while the modal remains open (e.g. the conversation changed)\",\"id\":\"AC-6\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, disconnected-opener guard)\",\"then\":\"no error is thrown and focus is not restored to a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to body, matching today's behaviour)\",\"when\":\"the modal is closed and unmounts\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is mounted\",\"id\":\"AC-7\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape)\",\"then\":\"onClose is called exactly once — the single-call Escape close behaviour is unchanged\",\"when\":\"an Escape keydown is dispatched on document\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is mounted\",\"id\":\"AC-8\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (close button onClick)\",\"then\":\"onClose is called — close-button close behaviour is unchanged\",\"when\":\"the close button (accessible name 'Close') is clicked\"},{\"given\":\"the citation modal is mounted\",\"id\":\"AC-9\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (backdrop onClick, e.target === e.currentTarget)\",\"then\":\"onClose is called for the backdrop click only — backdrop close behaviour is unchanged\",\"when\":\"the backdrop overlay is clicked (and clicks inside the dialog body are stopped from closing)\"},{\"given\":\"the modal is mounted with a citation whose video_url has a valid v parameter\",\"id\":\"AC-10\",\"kind\":\"guard\",\"seam\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (iframe embedUrl + externalUrl derivation)\",\"then\":\"video playback and timestamp links are unchanged: the YouTube iframe src embeds the video id with start=<startSeconds>&autoplay=1, and the 'Open on YouTube' external link carries t=<startSeconds>s\",\"when\":\"it renders\"}],\"dependencies\":[],\"invariants\":[\"The opener is captured from document.activeElement before focus is moved to the close button, within the same mount effect, so the modal's own focus-entry target can never become the restore target.\",\"Focus restoration happens only when the captured opener is an HTMLElement still connected to the document (el.isConnected); otherwise the cleanup is a no-op and no detached node is focused.\",\"No focus trap is added; Tab behaviour beyond focus entry and focus return is unchanged.\",\"Production changes are confined to app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx; Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, the backend, authentication, owner-private conversation handling and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\",\"Existing close paths (Escape, close button, backdrop), body scroll lock, iframe/external URL derivation and transcript-snippet rendering keep their current code and tests.\",\"No new dependencies are introduced: vitest, @testing-library/react and @testing-library/jest-dom are already installed in app/frontend.\"],\"issue\":{\"number\":189,\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\"},\"out_of_scope\":[\"No focus trap (Tab cycling constrained to the dialog) — the acceptance criteria require entry and return only.\",\"No new dependencies such as focus-trap; no state-management additions.\",\"No Dynamous citation path changes — those citations bypass the modal via ChatArea.handleCitationClick and are unaffected.\",\"No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, backend changes, or factory authority/permission/proof-rule changes (issue hard constraints).\",\"No handling of real-browser iframe focus steal after the YouTube embed loads; browser e2e proof should assert focus immediately after open, before iframe settle.\"],\"risks\":[\"jsdom honours .focus()/document.activeElement so the seam is sound, but it cannot prove real-browser behaviour such as the YouTube iframe stealing focus after it loads.\",\"Restore-target drift: activeElement is captured in a post-paint effect, so if other code moved focus between the click and the effect, restore could target the wrong element. Accepted — nothing in the current app does so, and capture-then-focus ordering keeps this change's own focus move out of the failure mode.\",\"The focus-entry seam selects the close button by accessible name 'Close'; renaming that label would break the seam (the name is also the accessibility contract).\",\"Focusing the close button means Enter/Space now close the modal from the initial focus position; Escape still hits the document listener exactly once, as pinned by the existing test.\"],\"summary\":\"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: on mount, move keyboard focus to the in-dialog close button; on unmount, restore focus to the element that had focus when the modal opened (the citation chip), when that element is still connected to the document.\",\"version\":\"2.0\"}\n"},"task-contract.raw.json":{"sha256":"8dcea7ddc24aa4f0054139e0a675f22250a5531d75eb834f88384ab35c0ebf7e","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"issue\": {\"number\": 189, \"title\": \"Citation inspection [keyboard]\"},\n  \"summary\": \"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: on mount, move keyboard focus to the in-dialog close button; on unmount, restore focus to the element that had focus when the modal opened (the citation chip), when that element is still connected to the document.\",\n  \"behaviors\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"given\": \"the citation modal is mounted, having been opened from a citation chip button that currently has keyboard focus\", \"when\": \"CitationModal renders\", \"then\": \"keyboard focus is on the in-dialog close button (role 'button', accessible name 'Close'), a usable control inside the aria-modal dialog, not left on the chip behind the dialog\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"given\": \"the citation modal is mounted for a citation whose video_url yields no usable v parameter (the 'Video unavailable' path: no iframe and no 'Open on YouTube' link rendered)\", \"when\": \"CitationModal renders\", \"then\": \"the close button still receives keyboard focus — focus-entry does not depend on the iframe or external link being present\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"given\": \"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it (chip + modal rendered together, mirroring ChatArea's wiring)\", \"when\": \"the modal is closed via Escape (document keydown Escape → onClose → modal unmounts)\", \"then\": \"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"given\": \"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it\", \"when\": \"the modal is closed via the × close button click\", \"then\": \"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"given\": \"a citation chip button has keyboard focus and the modal was opened from it\", \"when\": \"the modal is closed via a backdrop click (click on the outer overlay, not the dialog body)\", \"then\": \"the opener chip button has keyboard focus again\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"given\": \"the opener chip button has been removed from the document while the modal remains open (e.g. the conversation changed)\", \"when\": \"the modal is closed and unmounts\", \"then\": \"no error is thrown and focus is not restored to a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to body, matching today's behaviour)\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, disconnected-opener guard)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"kind\": \"guard\", \"given\": \"the citation modal is mounted\", \"when\": \"an Escape keydown is dispatched on document\", \"then\": \"onClose is called exactly once — the single-call Escape close behaviour is unchanged\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"kind\": \"guard\", \"given\": \"the citation modal is mounted\", \"when\": \"the close button (accessible name 'Close') is clicked\", \"then\": \"onClose is called — close-button close behaviour is unchanged\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (close button onClick)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-9\", \"kind\": \"guard\", \"given\": \"the citation modal is mounted\", \"when\": \"the backdrop overlay is clicked (and clicks inside the dialog body are stopped from closing)\", \"then\": \"onClose is called for the backdrop click only — backdrop close behaviour is unchanged\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (backdrop onClick, e.target === e.currentTarget)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"kind\": \"guard\", \"given\": \"the modal is mounted with a citation whose video_url has a valid v parameter\", \"when\": \"it renders\", \"then\": \"video playback and timestamp links are unchanged: the YouTube iframe src embeds the video id with start=<startSeconds>&autoplay=1, and the 'Open on YouTube' external link carries t=<startSeconds>s\", \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (iframe embedUrl + externalUrl derivation)\"}\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"The opener is captured from document.activeElement before focus is moved to the close button, within the same mount effect, so the modal's own focus-entry target can never become the restore target.\",\n    \"Focus restoration happens only when the captured opener is an HTMLElement still connected to the document (el.isConnected); otherwise the cleanup is a no-op and no detached node is focused.\",\n    \"No focus trap is added; Tab behaviour beyond focus entry and focus return is unchanged.\",\n    \"Production changes are confined to app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx; Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, the backend, authentication, owner-private conversation handling and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\",\n    \"Existing close paths (Escape, close button, backdrop), body scroll lock, iframe/external URL derivation and transcript-snippet rendering keep their current code and tests.\",\n    \"No new dependencies are introduced: vitest, @testing-library/react and @testing-library/jest-dom are already installed in app/frontend.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"No focus trap (Tab cycling constrained to the dialog) — the acceptance criteria require entry and return only.\",\n    \"No new dependencies such as focus-trap; no state-management additions.\",\n    \"No Dynamous citation path changes — those citations bypass the modal via ChatArea.handleCitationClick and are unaffected.\",\n    \"No new content sources, sharing, auth changes, backend changes, or factory authority/permission/proof-rule changes (issue hard constraints).\",\n    \"No handling of real-browser iframe focus steal after the YouTube embed loads; browser e2e proof should assert focus immediately after open, before iframe settle.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"jsdom honours .focus()/document.activeElement so the seam is sound, but it cannot prove real-browser behaviour such as the YouTube iframe stealing focus after it loads.\",\n    \"Restore-target drift: activeElement is captured in a post-paint effect, so if other code moved focus between the click and the effect, restore could target the wrong element. Accepted — nothing in the current app does so, and capture-then-focus ordering keeps this change's own focus move out of the failure mode.\",\n    \"The focus-entry seam selects the close button by accessible name 'Close'; renaming that label would break the seam (the name is also the accessibility contract).\",\n    \"Focusing the close button means Enter/Space now close the modal from the initial focus position; Escape still hits the document listener exactly once, as pinned by the existing test.\"\n  ],\n  \"ambiguities\": [],\n  \"dependencies\": []\n}\n"},"ticket.json":{"sha256":"5d8fbab973959533562b0e61687d978fd962f97ce65aa66294a1141e7240945d","text":"{\"acceptance\":[\"AC-1\",\"AC-2\",\"AC-3\",\"AC-4\",\"AC-5\",\"AC-6\",\"AC-7\",\"AC-8\",\"AC-9\",\"AC-10\"],\"body_sha256\":\"c9ab4b6c10b1bc2e22dce3602ffde023c2d6c26cb885a9df12e56b7c665ec56a\",\"contract_sha256\":\"8d3107a78e3f12727a0f2996edbd07a6065e665ddeb933fbc1f59b696b2f7093\",\"issue\":189,\"parent\":null,\"test_seams\":{\"AC-1\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\",\"AC-10\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (iframe embedUrl + externalUrl derivation)\",\"AC-2\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\",\"AC-3\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"AC-4\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"AC-5\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, opener restore)\",\"AC-6\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup, disconnected-opener guard)\",\"AC-7\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape)\",\"AC-8\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (close button onClick)\",\"AC-9\":\"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (backdrop onClick, e.target === e.currentTarget)\"},\"title\":\"Citation inspection [keyboard]\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"}},"base_sha":"fa2b38585181be98f6063daaa4e5d601c5737c9c","issue":189,"issue_sha256":"ee04b5def8b555b9255e81078bb4c0444cd97041719b3cd3792efab4e1010628","kernel_commit":"fa2b38585181be98f6063daaa4e5d601c5737c9c","note_ref":"refs/notes/dark-factory-carry","policy_sha256":"69075d8c1f8600378a9a89bf02b686df7e9